<title>FRANCE: Indian strike little impact on Air France.</title>
<headline>Indian strike little impact on Air France.</headline>
<text>
<p>PARIS, April 14 - Air France said a strike by Indian air traffic controllers last weekend did not have a significant impact on its cargo activities.</p>
<p>The strike was called off around 1130 GMT Saturday April 12.</p>
<p>&quot;None of our Boeing 747-200 freighters were blocked in India because of the strike and we simply cancelled scheduled cargo services serving the country. The result was only a minor effect on our Indian traffic,&quot; an Air France Cargo official told Reuters.</p>
<p>Air France operates scheduled 747F services between Paris/CDG and New Delhi, Bangalore and Madras. - Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017</p>
